# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# fine-video-as-code — local environment template
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your real values:
#   cp .env.example .env       (macOS/Linux)
#   copy .env.example .env     (Windows)
#
# `.env` is gitignored. `.env.example` is committed as a template.
# The dev/start scripts load `.env` automatically via
# `node --env-file=.env`.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── LLM (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Step 1 optionally rewrites the voiceover text with an LLM
# when the topic comes from the form. If unset, the templates
# fall back to per-role canned text — the pipeline still works,
# just less polished.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint works:
#   OpenAI, Anthropic (via gateway), Alibaba DashScope
#   compatible-mode, Ollama, vLLM, lm-studio, etc.
#
# Example 1 — MiniMax (recommended, OpenAI-compatible):
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.minimax.io/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=MiniMax-M3
#   LLM_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here
#   Get your key at https://platform.minimax.io/console/plan
#   MiniMax also exposes an Anthropic-compatible endpoint at
#   https://api.minimax.io/anthropic if you prefer that path.
#
# Example 2 — OpenAI:
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# Example 3 — Alibaba Qwen via DashScope compatible-mode:
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=qwen-plus
#
# Example 4 — Local Ollama:
#   LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
#   LLM_API_KEY=ollama
#
# Example 5 — Disable LLM (use template-only):
#   leave all three blank

# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.minimax.io/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-replace-me
# LLM_MODEL=MiniMax-M3
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=30000


# ── Server (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT=3000


# ── Render engine (optional) ─────────────────────────────────
# 0 = realtime (page.video() webm, faster on slow machines)
# 1 = deterministic (per-frame screenshot, bit-reproducible)
# Default is 1 — change only if rendering is too slow.
# DETERMINISTIC_RENDER=1


# ── Playwright sandbox (optional) ────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 when running inside a container that lacks the
# privileges Chromium needs for its default sandbox.
# PLAYWRIGHT_NO_SANDBOX=0
